---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy of New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG.">
    
    <section class="bg-linear-to-b from-teal-950/40 via-background to-background pt-20 pb-12 text-center relative border-b border-border/40">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary tracking-wider uppercase mb-2 block">🔒 Your Data, Your Rights</span>
            <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
                How New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG collects, uses, and protects your personal data in accordance with GDPR regulations.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted-foreground/60 mt-3 font-medium">Last updated: May 27, 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground space-y-6">
            
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG</strong> ("we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring that your personal data is handled in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Irish data protection law. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and protect your personal information when you interact with our services, website, events, and programs.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">2. Data Controller</h2>
            <p>
                New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG is the data controller responsible for your personal information. If you have any questions or wish to exercise your data protection rights, you can contact us at: 
                <a href="mailto:info@lifeintegration.ie" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">info@lifeintegration.ie</a>.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">3. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>We may collect and process the following categories of personal data:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Name, email address, phone number, and city/location.</li>
                <li><strong>Program Participation Data:</strong> Event registration details, leadership program applications, branch interest forms, languages spoken, background, and experience.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical & Usage Data:</strong> IP address, browser type and version, device information, operating system, and website usage data collected via cookies and scripts.</li>
                <li><strong>Communication Data:</strong> Records of your interactions when you contact us via contact forms, registration forms, or email subscriptions.</li>
                <li><strong>Payment Information:</strong> Processed entirely through secure third-party payment processors. We do not store your full payment details on our systems.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">4. Third-Party Service Providers (Subprocessors)</h2>
            <p>To run our platform securely and efficiently, we partner with reliable third-party services that process data in compliance with GDPR:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> We use Cloudflare for web performance, content delivery (CDN), and security optimization. Cloudflare processes basic technical logs (IP addresses, system configuration) to block malicious traffic and accelerate page load speeds.</li>
                <li><strong>Brevo:</strong> We use Brevo as our marketing automation and communication platform. When you subscribe to our newsletter, submit a contact form, or sign up for a program, your contact details are securely stored on Brevo's servers to handle notifications and emails.</li>
                <li><strong>Google Tag Manager & Google Analytics:</strong> We use Google Tag Manager to manage deployment scripts, and Google Analytics to collect anonymized website usage statistics. These tools help us track user behavior and improve website performance without identifying individuals.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">5. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>We use your personal data for the following purposes:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><strong>Service Delivery:</strong> To register you for events, programmes, and workshops, and to deliver our services to you.</li>
                <li><strong>Communication:</strong> To communicate with you about our services, events, activities, and to respond to your enquiries.</li>
                <li><strong>Marketing:</strong> To send you updates and newsletters via Brevo, provided you have explicitly opted in.</li>
                <li><strong>Administration:</strong> To process branch applications, manage branch operations, and administer our organisation.</li>
                <li><strong>Optimization & Security:</strong> To monitor and secure our website traffic through Cloudflare and analyze engagement via Google Analytics.</li>
                <li><strong>Legal Compliance:</strong> To comply with legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">6. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
            <p>We process your personal data on the following legal bases under the GDPR:</p>
            <p><strong>Consent:</strong> Where you have given clear consent for us to process your personal data for a specific purpose, such as subscribing to our newsletter or accepting analytics cookies.</p>
            <p><strong>Contract:</strong> Where processing is necessary for the performance of a contract with you, such as event registration or programme enrolment.</p>
            <p><strong>Legitimate Interests:</strong> Where processing is necessary for our legitimate interests, provided your rights and interests do not override them. This includes improving our web infrastructure via Cloudflare, analyzing performance, and maintaining system security.</p>
            <p><strong>Legal Obligation:</strong> Where processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation, such as maintaining financial or organizational records.</p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">7. Data Sharing</h2>
            <p>
                We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal data to third parties. We may share relevant operational data with <strong>Branch Leaders</strong> where you have registered for events at a specific branch. We also share data with our verified <strong>Service Providers</strong> (like Brevo and Cloudflare) who are contractually obligated to protect your data under strict Data Processing Agreements (DPA).
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">8. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>
                We retain your personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected, including for the purposes of satisfying any legal, accounting, or reporting requirements.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">9. Data Security</h2>
            <p>
                We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data against unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. These measures include SSL/TLS encryption via Cloudflare, restricted access controls, and secure integration with Brevo. However, no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">10. Your Rights</h2>
            <p>
                Under GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, or erase your personal data ("Right to be forgotten"), as well as the right to object to or restrict processing. You can withdraw your consent at any time (e.g., via the "Unsubscribe" link in any Brevo email). Simply reach out to us at <a href="mailto:info@lifeintegration.ie" class="text-primary hover:underline">info@lifeintegration.ie</a> to submit a request. We will respond within one month.
            </p>
            <p>
                You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Commission (DPC), Ireland's supervisory authority for data protection (<a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">www.dataprotection.ie</a>).
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">11. Cookies & Consent Management</h2>
            <p>
                Our website uses cookies to enhance your browsing experience. Essential cookies (like those used by Cloudflare for security) do not require consent. Analytics and tracking cookies (like those managed by Google Tag Manager) will only be activated if you explicitly grant permission via our Cookie Consent Banner.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

</Layout>